    'Broken access control resulting from platform misconfiguration' => 'Celah kontrol akses akibat salah konfigurasi platform',
    "Some applications enforce access controls at the platform layer. they do this by restricting access to specific URLs and HTTP methods based on the user's role. For example, an application might configure a rule as follows:" => 'Sebagian aplikasi memasang aturan kontrol akses di lapisan platform berdasarkan kombinasi URL dan metode HTTP per peran pengguna:',
    'This rule denies access to the [[C0]] method on the URL [[C1]], for users in the managers group. Various things can go wrong in this situation, leading to access control bypasses.' => 'Aturan tersebut menolak metode [[C0]] ke URL [[C1]] bagi grup managers, namun banyak celah implementasi bisa melewatinya.',
    'Some application frameworks support various non-standard HTTP headers that can be used to override the URL in the original request, such as [[C0]] and [[C1]]. If a website uses rigorous front-end controls to restrict access based on the URL, but the application allows the URL to be overridden via a request header, then it might be possible to bypass the access controls using a request like the following:' => 'Framework tertentu mendukung header seperti [[C0]] atau [[C1]] untuk menimpa path rute. Jika proxy front-end hanya mengecek path permintaan awal, pembatasan mudah dilewati lewat header tersebut:',
    'An alternative attack relates to the HTTP method used in the request. The front-end controls described in the previous sections restrict access based on the URL and HTTP method. Some websites tolerate different HTTP request methods when performing an action. If an attacker can use the [[C0]] (or another) method to perform actions on a restricted URL, they can bypass the access control that is implemented at the platform layer.' => 'Cara lain adalah mengganti metode HTTP. Jika aturan hanya memblokir POST sementara aplikasi tetap memproses metode [[C0]] atau metode lain, kontrol akses front-end dapat ditembus.',
    'Broken access control resulting from URL-matching discrepancies' => 'Celah kontrol akses akibat selisih pencocokan URL',
    'Websites can vary in how strictly they match the path of an incoming request to a defined endpoint. For example, they may tolerate inconsistent capitalization, so a request to [[C0]] may still be mapped to the [[C1]] endpoint. If the access control mechanism is less tolerant, it may treat these as two different endpoints and fail to enforce the correct restrictions as a result.' => 'Jika rute aplikasi mengabaikan huruf besar-kecil sehingga [[C0]] dipetakan ke [[C1]], sementara pemeriksaan akses peka huruf besar-kecil, aturan pembatasan menjadi gugur.',
    'Similar discrepancies can arise if developers using the Spring framework have enabled the [[C0]] option. This allows paths with an arbitrary file extension to be mapped to an equivalent endpoint with no file extension. In other words, a request to [[C1]] would still match the [[C2]] pattern. Prior to Spring 5.3, this option is enabled by default.' => 'Pada framework Spring dengan opsi [[C0]], penambahan ekstensi seperti [[C1]] tetap dipetakan ke [[C2]] dan berisiko melewati aturan berbasis pola URL.',
    'On other systems, you may encounter discrepancies in whether [[C0]] and [[C1]] are treated as distinct endpoints. In this case, you may be able to bypass access controls by appending a trailing slash to the path.' => 'Perbedaan perlakuan terhadap garis miring akhir antara [[C0]] dan [[C1]] juga kerap dapat dimanfaatkan untuk melewati kontrol akses.',
    'Horizontal privilege escalation' => 'Eskalasi hak istimewa horizontal',
    'Horizontal privilege escalation occurs if a user is able to gain access to resources belonging to another user, instead of their own resources of that type. For example, if an employee can access the records of other employees as well as their own, then this is horizontal privilege escalation.' => 'Eskalasi hak istimewa horizontal terjadi saat pengguna bisa mengakses data atau fitur milik pengguna lain yang setara.',
    'Horizontal privilege escalation attacks may use similar types of exploit methods to vertical privilege escalation. For example, a user might access their own account page using the following URL:' => 'Serangannya sering memakai teknik serupa, misalnya halaman akun diakses lewat URL berikut:',
    'If an attacker modifies the [[C0]] parameter value to that of another user, they might gain access to another user\'s account page, and the associated data and functions.' => 'Jika penyerang mengganti parameter [[C0]] menjadi ID pengguna lain, data dan fungsi akun korban dapat terbuka.',
    'This is an example of an insecure direct object reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This type of vulnerability arises where user-controller parameter values are used to access resources or functions directly.' => 'Ini adalah contoh kerentanan IDOR (insecure direct object reference), ketika parameter kendali pengguna dipakai langsung mengambil objek.',
    'In some applications, the exploitable parameter does not have a predictable value. For example, instead of an incrementing number, an application might use globally unique identifiers (GUIDs) to identify users. This may prevent an attacker from guessing or predicting another user\'s identifier. However, the GUIDs belonging to other users might be disclosed elsewhere in the application where users are referenced, such as user messages or reviews.' => 'Walaupun aplikasi memakai GUID acak ketimbang angka berurutan, GUID pengguna lain tetap sering bocor di fitur publik seperti ulasan atau pesan.',
    'In some cases, an application does detect when the user is not permitted to access the resource, and returns a redirect to the login page. However, the response containing the redirect might still include some sensitive data belonging to the targeted user, so the attack is still successful.' => 'Terkadang aplikasi memang mengembalikan redirect ke halaman login saat akses ditolak, namun tetap menyertakan data sensitif di dalam body respons redirect tersebut.',
    'Horizontal to vertical privilege escalation' => 'Eskalasi horizontal menuju vertikal',
    'Often, a horizontal privilege escalation attack can be turned into a vertical privilege escalation, by compromising a more privileged user. For example, a horizontal escalation might allow an attacker to reset or capture the password belonging to another user. If the attacker targets an administrative user and compromises their account, then they can gain administrative access and so perform vertical privilege escalation.' => 'Eskalasi horizontal kerap berubah menjadi vertikal bila target yang diambil alih adalah akun admin sehingga penyerang memperoleh seluruh hak administratif.',
    'An attacker might be able to gain access to another user\'s account page using the parameter tampering technique already described for horizontal privilege escalation:' => 'Penyerang dapat mengarahkan manipulasi parameter akun ke ID milik administrator:',
    "If the target user is an application administrator, then the attacker will gain access to an administrative account page. This page might disclose the administrator's password or provide a means of changing it, or might provide direct access to privileged functionality." => 'Jika akun tersebut adalah administrator, halaman akunnya dapat membocorkan kredensial admin atau memberi akses langsung ke fitur istimewa.',
    'Insecure direct object references' => 'Insecure direct object references (IDOR)',
    'Insecure direct object references (IDORs) are a subcategory of access control vulnerabilities. IDORs occur if an application uses user-supplied input to access objects directly and an attacker can modify the input to obtain unauthorized access. It was popularized by its appearance in the OWASP 2007 Top Ten. It\'s just one example of many implementation mistakes that can provide a means to bypass access controls.' => 'Insecure direct object references (IDOR) adalah subkategori celah kontrol akses yang terjadi ketika aplikasi memakai input pengguna untuk mengakses objek secara langsung tanpa memverifikasi kepemilikan atau otorisasi, sehingga penyerang dapat memanipulasi input untuk memperoleh akses tidak sah.',
    'Insecure direct object references (IDOR)' => 'Insecure direct object references (IDOR)',
    'Access control vulnerabilities in multi-step processes' => 'Celah kontrol akses pada proses bertahap',
    'Many websites implement important functions over a series of steps. This is common when:' => 'Banyak fitur penting dipecah menjadi beberapa langkah berurutan, misalnya ketika:',
    'A variety of inputs or options need to be captured.' => 'Banyak input atau opsi harus dikumpulkan.',
    'The user needs to review and confirm details before the action is performed.' => 'Pengguna perlu meninjau dan mengonfirmasi detail sebelum aksi dijalankan.',
    'For example, the administrative function to update user details might involve the following steps:' => 'Misalnya proses admin memperbarui data pengguna melewati tiga tahap:',
    'Load the form that contains details for a specific user.' => 'Memuat formulir detail pengguna.',
    'Submit the changes.' => 'Mengirim perubahan.',
    'Review the changes and confirm.' => 'Meninjau perubahan lalu mengonfirmasi.',
    'Sometimes, a website will implement rigorous access controls over some of these steps, but ignore others. Imagine a website where access controls are correctly applied to the first and second steps, but not to the third step. The website assumes that a user will only reach step 3 if they have already completed the first steps, which are properly controlled. An attacker can gain unauthorized access to the function by skipping the first two steps and directly submitting the request for the third step with the required parameters.' => 'Jika kontrol akses hanya dipasang di langkah awal dan lalai memeriksa ulang pada langkah akhir, penyerang dapat langsung mengirim permintaan ke langkah konfirmasi akhir.',
    'Referer-based access control' => 'Kontrol akses berbasis Referer',
    'Some websites base access controls on the [[C0]] header submitted in the HTTP request. The [[C1]] header can be added to requests by browsers to indicate which page initiated a request.' => 'Sebagian situs mengandalkan header HTTP [[C0]] dalam permintaan sebagai dasar kontrol akses. Header [[C1]] ini dapat ditambahkan browser ke permintaan untuk menunjukkan halaman yang memicu permintaan tersebut.',
    'For example, an application robustly enforces access control over the main administrative page at [[C0]], but for sub-pages such as [[C1]] only inspects the [[C2]] header. If the [[C3]] header contains the main [[C4]] URL, then the request is allowed.' => 'Misalnya halaman utama [[C0]] dilindungi ketat, namun sub-halaman [[C1]] hanya mengecek apakah header [[C2]] berasal dari [[C4]] (pemeriksaan [[C3]] ini sangat rapuh).',
    'In this case, the [[C0]] header can be fully controlled by an attacker. This means that they can forge direct requests to sensitive sub-pages by supplying the required [[C1]] header, and gain unauthorized access.' => 'Karena header [[C0]] dapat dipalsukan bebas oleh penyerang, menyuplai [[C1]] palsu cukup untuk menembus sub-halaman sensitif.',
    'Location-based access control' => 'Kontrol akses berbasis lokasi',
    "Some websites enforce access controls based on the user's geographical location. This can apply, for example, to banking applications or media services where state legislation or business restrictions apply. These access controls can often be circumvented by the use of web proxies, VPNs, or manipulation of client-side geolocation mechanisms." => 'Pembatasan berbasis lokasi geografis sering dapat dilewati memakai proxy web, VPN, atau manipulasi data geolokasi sisi klien.',
    'How to prevent access control vulnerabilities' => 'Cara mencegah kerentanan kontrol akses',
    'Access control vulnerabilities can be prevented by taking a defense-in-depth approach and applying the following principles:' => 'Kerentanan kontrol akses dapat dicegah dengan pendekatan pertahanan berlapis dan prinsip berikut:',
    'Never rely on obfuscation alone for access control.' => 'Jangan mengandalkan penyembunyian URL semata sebagai kontrol akses.',
    'Unless a resource is intended to be publicly accessible, deny access by default.' => 'Terapkan kebijakan tolak secara default untuk semua sumber daya selain yang memang publik.',
    'Wherever possible, use a single application-wide mechanism for enforcing access controls.' => 'Gunakan satu mekanisme otorisasi terpusat di seluruh aplikasi.',
    'At the code level, make it mandatory for developers to declare the access that is allowed for each resource, and deny access by default.' => 'Wajibkan deklarasi izin eksplisit pada level kode untuk tiap rute/sumber daya dengan kegagalan otomatis ke status ditolak.',
    'Thoroughly audit and test access controls to ensure they work as designed.' => 'Audit dan uji kontrol akses di setiap endpoint beserta setiap langkah alur kerja.',

    // security-models
    'In this section we explain what access control security models are and we discuss the most commonly encountered models.' => 'Pada bagian ini kami menjelaskan apa itu model keamanan kontrol akses beserta model yang paling umum ditemui.',
    'What are access control security models?' => 'Apa itu model keamanan kontrol akses?',
    'An access control security model is a formally defined definition of a set of access control rules that is independent of technology or implementation platform. Access control security models are implemented within operating systems, networks, database management systems and back office, application and web server software. Various access control security models have been devised over the years to match access control policies to business or organizational rules and changes in technology.' => 'Model keamanan kontrol akses adalah kerangka aturan otorisasi formal yang tidak terikat pada teknologi tertentu dan diterapkan di sistem operasi, jaringan, basis data, maupun aplikasi web.',
    'Programmatic access control' => 'Kontrol akses programatik',
    'With programmatic access control, a matrix of user privileges is stored in a database or similar and access controls are applied programmatically with reference to this matrix. This approach to access control can include roles or groups or individual users, collections or workflows of processes and can be highly granular.' => 'Matriks hak istimewa disimpan dalam database atau konfigurasi lalu diterapkan oleh kode aplikasi secara granular hingga tingkat individu, peran, dan alur proses.',
    'Discretionary access control (DAC)' => 'Discretionary access control (DAC)',
    'With discretionary access control, access to resources or functions is constrained based upon users or named groups of users. Owners of resources or functions have the ability to assign or delegate access permissions to users. This model is highly granular with access rights defined to an individual resource or function and user. Consequently the model can become very complex to design and manage.' => 'Dalam model DAC, pemilik sumber daya atau fungsi berhak menetapkan serta mendelegasikan izin akses ke pengguna atau grup tertentu. Model ini sangat terperinci tetapi bisa menjadi rumit dikelola.',
    'Mandatory access control (MAC)' => 'Mandatory access control (MAC)',
    'Mandatory access control is a centrally controlled system of access control in which access to some object (a file or other resource) by a subject is constrained. Significantly, unlike DAC the users and owners of resources have no capability to delegate or modify access rights for their resources. This model is often associated with military clearance-based systems.' => 'MAC dikendalikan terpusat berdasarkan tingkat otorisasi; pemilik objek tidak dapat mengubah atau mendelegasikan hak aksesnya, seperti sistem klasifikasi keamanan tinggi.',
    'Role-based access control (RBAC)' => 'Role-based access control (RBAC)',
    'With role-based access control, named roles are defined to which access privileges are assigned. Users are then assigned to single or multiple roles. RBAC provides enhanced management over other access control models and if properly designed sufficient granularity to provide manageable access control in complex applications. For example, the purchase clerk might be defined as a role with access permissions for a subset of purchase ledger functionality and resources. As employees leave or join an organization then access control management is simplified to defining or revoking membership of the purchases clerk role.' => 'Pada RBAC, izin dikelompokkan ke peran bernama lalu pengguna diberi satu atau beberapa peran. Manajemen izin di organisasi besar jauh lebih mudah karena cukup menambah atau mencabut peran pengguna.',
    'RBAC is most effective when there are sufficient roles to properly invoke access controls but not so many as to make the model excessively complex and unwieldy to manage.' => 'RBAC bekerja paling efektif saat jumlah peran cukup mewakili pemisahan tugas tanpa terlalu banyak hingga sulit dipelihara.',

    // idor
    'In this section, we will explain what insecure direct object references (IDOR) are and describe some common vulnerabilities.' => 'Pada bagian ini, kami menjelaskan apa itu insecure direct object references (IDOR) beserta contoh kerentanan yang umum terjadi.',
    'What are insecure direct object references (IDOR)?' => 'Apa itu insecure direct object references (IDOR)?',
    'Insecure direct object references (IDOR) are a type of access control vulnerability that arises when an application uses user-supplied input to access objects directly. The term IDOR was popularized by its appearance in the OWASP 2007 Top Ten. However, it is just one example of many access control implementation mistakes that can lead to access controls being circumvented. IDOR vulnerabilities are most commonly associated with horizontal privilege escalation, but they can also arise in relation to vertical privilege escalation.' => 'IDOR terjadi ketika aplikasi langsung memakai pengenal dari input pengguna untuk mengambil objek (record basis data atau file) tanpa mengecek apakah pengguna berhak mengaksesnya.',
    'IDOR examples' => 'Contoh celah IDOR',
    'There are many examples of access control vulnerabilities where user-controlled parameter values are used to access resources or functions directly.' => 'Berikut beberapa pola umum penggunaan parameter kendali pengguna untuk merujuk objek secara langsung.',
    'IDOR vulnerability with direct reference to database objects' => 'IDOR dengan rujukan langsung ke objek database',
    'Consider a website that uses the following URL to access the customer account page, by retrieving information from the back-end database:' => 'Misalkan aplikasi mengakses halaman akun pelanggan memakai URL berikut:',
    'Here, the customer number is used directly as a record index in queries that are performed on the back-end database. If no other controls are in place, an attacker can simply modify the [[C0]] value, bypassing access controls to view the records of other customers. This is an example of an IDOR vulnerability leading to horizontal privilege escalation.' => 'Parameter [[C0]] dipakai langsung pada query database; tanpa cek otorisasi, menggantinya akan menampilkan data milik pelanggan lain.',
    "An attacker might be able to perform horizontal and vertical privilege escalation by altering the user to one with additional privileges while bypassing access controls. Other possibilities include exploiting password leakage or modifying parameters once the attacker has landed in the user's accounts page, for example." => 'Jika objek yang dirujuk milik pengguna berhak tinggi, celah ini juga dapat membuka akses ke data sensitif atau fitur administratif.',
